From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] topology: do not let ambiguous snapshots move a client

An Agent can retain an associated station after that station has reassociated
elsewhere without sending a disassociation frame.  This is especially visible
during a complete RF outage: the destination Agent publishes the authoritative
Client Association Event, but the isolated source Agent still has the old
station in its local driver table.  When that Agent rejoins, its Associated
Clients TLV is a stale snapshot.  The topology-response repair path treated the
snapshot as a new association and evicted the newer, notification-owned row.

An Associated Clients TLV has no transaction ordering that can resolve two
simultaneous claims.  Before using a Topology Response to create an association,
scan the controller's per-device models.  If another device still has an
associated claim for the same STA on another BSS, retain the current owner and
wait for an unambiguous association event or snapshot.  Exact same-BSS reports
remain idempotent and a response can still repair a genuinely missing client.

This preserves the existing authority boundary: a Client Association Event can
move ownership; an ambiguous periodic snapshot cannot reverse it.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 src/em/config/em_configuration.cpp | 33 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 33 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/em/config/em_configuration.cpp b/src/em/config/em_configuration.cpp
--- a/src/em/config/em_configuration.cpp
+++ b/src/em/config/em_configuration.cpp
@@ -2351,6 +2351,39 @@ int em_configuration_t::handle_topology_response_clients(unsigned char *buff,
                 memcpy(sta_info.bssid, bssid, sizeof(bssid_t));
                 memcpy(sta_info.radiomac, bss_info->ruid.mac, sizeof(mac_address_t));
                 sta_info.associated = true;
+
+                /* A Topology Response is an unordered snapshot.  If two
+                 * device models claim the same STA on different BSSs, it
+                 * cannot establish which association happened last.  Do not
+                 * let a rejoining Agent's stale driver row reverse the
+                 * authoritative Client Association Event from the current
+                 * owner. */
+                bool conflicting_claim = false;
+                dm_easy_mesh_t *claim_dm = get_mgr()->get_first_dm();
+                while (claim_dm != NULL && !conflicting_claim) {
+                    if (claim_dm != dm) {
+                        dm_sta_t *claim = claim_dm->get_first_sta(sta_info.id);
+                        while (claim != NULL) {
+                            if (claim->m_sta_info.associated &&
+                                    memcmp(claim->m_sta_info.bssid,
+                                           sta_info.bssid,
+                                           sizeof(bssid_t)) != 0) {
+                                conflicting_claim = true;
+                                break;
+                            }
+                            claim = claim_dm->get_next_sta(sta_info.id, claim);
+                        }
+                    }
+                    claim_dm = get_mgr()->get_next_dm(claim_dm);
+                }
+                if (conflicting_claim) {
+                    em_printfout(
+                            "Skipping ambiguous Topology Response owner for sta=%s bssid=%s",
+                            util::mac_to_string(sta_info.id).c_str(),
+                            util::mac_to_string(sta_info.bssid).c_str());
+                    continue;
+                }
+
                 if (dm->get_sta_info(sta_info.id, sta_info.bssid, sta_info.radiomac,
                                      em_target_sta_map_consolidated) != NULL) {
                     continue;
